                "retweet_count": 15,
                "source": "Twitter for iPhone",
                "text": "Trump and Republican cuts to Medicaid, known as NJ Family Cares in New Jersey, will negatively impact communicates across the entire state. It will take time to feel this exact impact, but make no mistake: hospitals, nursing homes, and healthcare providers are preparing for these cuts now.\n \nHere are just some ways we can expect to see NJ families affected.\n\n- 350,000 eligible New Jerseyans will lose their coverage. That\u2019s 1 out of every 5 covered residents. \n\n- $3.3 billion will be cut for hospitals and public health. Hospitals may need to cut staff, services, or even shut down entirely. \n\n- $360 million cut from the state budget due to restrictions in federal funding.",
